1
00:00:02,020 --> 00:00:02,660
Reading

2
00:00:03,880 --> 00:00:06,380
The Road to Modern English

3
00:00:07,240 --> 00:00:12,680
At the end of the 16th century, about five to seven million people spoke English.

4
00:00:13,340 --> 00:00:15,540
Nearly all of them lived in England.

5
00:00:16,580 --> 00:00:18,180
Later in the next century,

6
00:00:18,420 --> 00:00:22,100
people from England made voyages to conquer other parts of the world

7
00:00:22,180 --> 00:00:26,920
and because of that, English began to be spoken in many other countries.

8
00:00:27,860 --> 00:00:31,100
Today, more people speak English as their first,

9
00:00:31,300 --> 00:00:34,740
second or a foreign language than ever before.

10
00:00:36,180 --> 00:00:41,040
Native English speakers can understand each other even if they don’t speak the same kind of English.

11
00:00:47,880 --> 00:00:49,980
I’d like to come up to your apartment.

12
00:00:51,880 --> 00:00:54,160
So why has English changed over time?

13
00:00:55,100 --> 00:00:59,320
Actually all languages change and develop when cultures meet

14
00:00:59,320 --> 00:01:01,080
and communicate with each other.

15
00:01:02,520 --> 00:01:06,400
At first the English spoken in England between about AD 450

16
00:01:06,400 --> 00:01:10,800
and 1150 was very different from the English spoken today.

17
00:01:11,560 --> 00:01:15,800
It was based more on German than the English we speak at present.

18
00:01:16,300 --> 00:01:20,760
Then gradually between about AD 800 and 1150,

19
00:01:20,920 --> 00:01:26,600
English became less like German because those who ruled England spoke first Danish

20
00:01:26,600 --> 00:01:27,980
and later French.

21
00:01:29,260 --> 00:01:34,140
These new settlers enriched the English language and especially its vocabulary.

22
00:01:44,440 --> 00:01:48,100
In 1620 some British settlers moved to America.

23
00:01:54,700 --> 00:01:57,420
English began to be spoken in both countries.

24
00:02:02,960 --> 00:02:06,340
At that time two big changes in English spelling happened:

25
00:02:07,340 --> 00:02:09,760
First, Samuel Johnson wrote his dictionary,

26
00:02:10,240 --> 00:02:13,500
and later Noah Webster wrote the American

27
00:02:13,500 --> 00:02:15,380
Dictionary of the English Language.

28
00:02:15,980 --> 00:02:21,380
The latter gave a separate identity to American English spelling.

29
00:02:22,500 --> 00:02:26,460
English now is also spoken as a foreign or second language in South Asia.

30
00:02:27,240 --> 00:02:31,780
For example, India has a very large number of fluent English speakers

31
00:02:31,780 --> 00:02:37,220
because Britain ruled India from 1765 to 1947.

32
00:02:38,540 --> 00:02:41,920
During that time English became the language for government

33
00:02:41,920 --> 00:02:42,880
and education.

34
00:02:52,380 --> 00:02:56,360
Today the number of people learning English in China is increasing rapidly.

35
00:02:57,100 --> 00:03:00,600
In fact, China may have the largest number of English learners.

36
00:03:01,540 --> 00:03:04,200
Will Chinese English develop its own identity?

37
00:03:04,940 --> 00:03:06,300
Only time will tell.
